+  // `display::features::kCtmColorManagement` is declared inside a
+  // `#if BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)` in ui/display/display_features.h, so off
+  // ChromeOS there is no flag to consult and the honest answer is the one a
+  // disabled flag gives -- here, the calibration profile's own matrix rather
+  // than one derived from the plane and output primaries. Measured, not read:
